  "body": "## What changed\n- `list_features` face rows: when `outward_normal` refuses (open or inside-out shell), `normal` and `facing` are null and `outside_unknown` holds the reason. Before, the row showed the canonical plane normal and a definite `facing`.\n- The listing still does not fail on one face. A closed shell is unchanged.\n- `camcraft-mcp` skill: the #937 caveat is replaced by a description of the new field.\n\nCause: `outward()` in `crates/app/src/mcp/features.rs` fell back to the canonical normal on refusal.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `mcp_list_features_outside::an_open_shell_face_says_its_outside_is_unknown`: null fields, named reason, and `lay_part_on_face` refuses the same face.\n- `mcp_list_features_outside::a_closed_box_keeps_its_outward_normals`.\n\nGate: those two, `mcp_wcs_features`, `mcp_lay_face`, `mcp_pick` pass. `clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\nNot exercised: the T-junction plate of the issue (an open shell by a dropped facet is used instead); full quick tier; no G-code or check verdict changes.\n\nProcess change: yes (the `camcraft-mcp` skill output shape).\n\nChangelog: `list_features` face rows give null `facing` and `normal` and an `outside_unknown` reason when the face's outside cannot be told.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2186\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
